{
  "schema": 1,
  "_readme": [
    "This file is DATA, not code. Edit it freely \u2014 `lane models` reads it live.",
    "Prices are USD per million tokens. `tier` is a 0-100 capability score used",
    "only for ranking within LANE; it is a judgement, not a benchmark result.",
    "",
    "Anything with pricing_verified: null is a STARTING GUESS. LANE will still",
    "route with it, but `lane doctor` warns, and savings figures that depend on",
    "it are marked estimated. Run `lane models --sync` to prune entries your",
    "keys cannot actually reach and to list models the provider offers that are",
    "missing here.",
    "sampling: false means the provider REJECTS temperature/top_p with a 400. The adapter strips them rather than forwarding what the client sent.",
    "groq/compound is deliberately ABSENT. G.I.L. measured it returning no content in streaming mode across three attempts; a model that silently answers nothing is worse than a missing one. Re-add it only once its tool-step response shape is handled.",
    "There is deliberately NO Anthropic image model. No Claude model generates images, and inventing one so the advisor always has an answer would make it confidently wrong on the exact request where being wrong is most obvious. When a site cannot do the job, the advisor says which one can.",
    "strengths is what separates the performance variation from a rate card. Tier says how good a model is; strengths say what it is good AT, so 'best for this request' can mean the fast model for a greeting and the thinking one for a proof."
  ],
